{"compatibility":"minor","safety_note_md":"# SafeStan Safety Note

Compatibility: minor.

Protected data: none. The only top-level data variable, `N`, is a size/configuration input and is not observed with a sampling statement.

Generated files: `model_safe.stan`, `data_safe.json`.

Changes: replaced the manual `target += normal_lpdf(...)` statements with equivalent built-in sampling statements. The conditional density for `y` was vectorized as `y ~ normal(theta, 1)`, and the prior for `theta` was placed before `y` so that `theta` is not used before its prior. The data were unchanged.
","model_safe_stan":"data {
  int<lower=1> N; // Number of ys, supplied by interface
}

parameters {
  array[N] real y;  // Probabilistic variables y
  real theta; // Probabilistic variable theta
}

model {
  // Add marginal probability density for theta
  // to the joint log probability density
  theta ~ normal(0, 1);

  // Add conditional probability density for the ys
  // given theta to the joint log probability density
  y ~ normal(theta, 1);
}
","data_safe_json":"{
  "N": 1
}","protected_variables":[]}
